  "releaseNotes": "Release Notes for ContainsContact Class on .net 9.0\n\t\tVersion: 2.0.11\n\t\tDate: March 22, 2025\n\n\t\tOverview:\n\t\tThe ContainsContact class is a static utility designed to validate whether a given input text contains sensitive or contact-related information. This release introduces additional validation to detect email addresses alongside previously existing checks for phone numbers, social media links, and inappropriate content.\n\n\t\tNew Features:\n\t\tEmail Address Detection:\n\t\tAdded detection for email addresses in the input text.\n\t\tIf an email address is found, the method returns a validation failure with the message: \"A text contains an email address.\".\n\t\tThe email validation utilizes a regular expression to match standard email formats (e.g., username@domain.com).\n\t\tImprovements:\n\t\tPhone Number Validation:\n\n\t\tContinues to detect phone numbers in both numeric formats (e.g., 123-456-7890) and text-based formats (e.g., one two three four).\n\t\tInappropriate Content Detection:\n\n\t\tThe class checks for and flags inappropriate content such as abusive language, hate speech, and sexual content based on predefined word patterns.\n\t\tSocial Media Link Detection:\n\n\t\tChecks for links to social media platforms and flags any detected contact information with a message specific to the platform.\n\t\tBug Fixes:\n\t\tNo bug fixes in this release.\n\t\tUsage:\n\t\tcsharp\n\t\tCopy\n\t\tvar result = ContainsContact.ContainsContact(\"Your input text here\");\n\t\tif (!result.isValid)\n\t\t{\n\t\tConsole.WriteLine($\"Invalid input: {result.validationMessage}\");\n\t\t}\n\t\telse\n\t\t{\n\t\tConsole.WriteLine(\"Text is valid.\");\n\t\t}\n\t\tImpact:\n\t\tThis release expands the functionality of the ContainsContact class to now include email address detection, in addition to existing validation for social media links, phone numbers, and inappropriate content.\n\n\t\tThe update is non-breaking, meaning it is fully compatible with existing implementations of the class.\n\n\t\tKnown Limitations:\n\t\tThe email validation pattern is designed for typical email formats but may not capture every possible variation.\n\t\tSocial media sites and inappropriate words are checked against predefined lists that might need to be updated periodically.\n\t\tEnd of Release Notes",
